{
 "village": "khiyana",
 "agent_notes": "Best lead: Khiyana is described (Hindi Wikipedia user essay + Jatland's Dhatarwal gotra page) as the origin/samadhi village of the Dhatarwal Jat clan's folk deity Nathu Dada (d. VS 1444 / 1387 CE), with a temple there drawing devotees from Rajasthan, Punjab and Haryana and an annual fair; one source says the village itself was founded by Khiyaji, Nathu Dada's second son, which conflicts slightly with Jatland's framing of Khiyana as Nathu's own place of origin \u2014 both are community/genealogy sources needing independent verification. Patrika (Bikaner desk) ran three 2018/2022 features on the 34-village Mahajan Field Firing Range displacement (1984-85 acquisition, resettlement in Khajuwala/Dantaur/Pugal/Mohangarh/Nachna) but NONE of the three name Khiyana specifically \u2014 they name Bhojrasar, Kumbhana, Motlai, Khanisar, Thoiyan, Mneran, Duder instead, so village-level displacement reporting on Khiyana is a gap. Census/village-directory portals (villageinfo.in, onefivenine.com) carry the surviving 'Kheenyera/Khinyera' revenue village (pop. 2,939, 483 households, area 1,920 ha) that the research unit's own notes equate with old Khiyana, but no external source states that equivalence explicitly. jatland.com and villageinfo.in/onefivenine.com blocked WebFetch (403) so only search-snippet text was usable for them, not full pages. YouTube, image-search, and indiankanoon/gazette queries returned nothing village-specific. A Facebook page named 'Khiyana' (~859 likes) turned up but is login-walled and its geography is unconfirmed \u2014 'Khiyana' is also an Arabic/Urdu word (betrayal), so it may be an unrelated homonym.",
 "searches_used": 20,
